{"parentUuid":"233bba02-d07f-4248-bd72-31da03dc6bdd","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01KhWWGBfCPJQA5a5VUutFqE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Fixed and shipped. **prime-silo v1.4.2 is released** — green across all platforms.\n\n## What went wrong with 1.4.0, and the fixes\nBoth were CI-only packaging bugs that my local Windows `desktop:pack` masked:\n\n1. **v1.4.0 failed (Linux/macOS):** `extraResources` copying `memoray/server/node_modules` hit `EEXIST` on the `node_modules/.bin/systeminformation` **symlink** — npm writes real symlinks on POSIX but shim files on Windows, so my local build never saw it. → Fix: `filter: [\"**/*\", \"!.bin/**\"]` (the `.bin` CLIs aren't needed at runtime).\n2. **v1.4.1 failed (Windows):** my build-time dep guard used `spawnSync(\"npm.cmd\", …)` without `shell:true`, which can't launch on Windows runners (exits `null`). → Fix: run it as a single shell command string with `shell:true`.\n\nEach fix was **verified on the platform that failed** before re-releasing — I even simulated a clean clone (removed `node_modules`) locally to exercise the Windows guard. Failed tags were deleted and the version bumped each time, per this repo's convention (the same pattern as v1.2.8→v1.2.9).\n\n## v1.4.2 — published\nRun concluded **success**, **15 assets**:\n- **Windows** x64 + arm64 `.exe`\n- **macOS** x64 + arm64 `.dmg` (+ updater zips)\n- **Linux** x64 + arm64 `.AppImage`\n- Auto-updater metadata `.yml` + the zero-install runtime bundle\n\nRelease: https://github.com/binary16labs/prime-silo/releases/tag/v1.4.2\n\nThe full memo-ray merge — all five native screens, earth-tone theme, adaptive linear/force graph, MCP, and the zero-install memo-ray bundle — is now live in a published prime-silo release. The standalone memo-ray repo remains untouched for anyone who wants it on its own.\n\nOne thing worth flagging for next time: `package.json` `build.publish` points at `agent0ai/space-agent`, but the tag published to your `binary16labs/prime-silo` origin (where the assets landed) — just so you know which repo's releases page is authoritative. The two cross-platform packaging lessons are saved to memory."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":459,"cache_creation_input_tokens":911,"cache_read_input_tokens":581268,"output_tokens":800,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":911,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":459,"output_tokens":800,"cache_read_input_tokens":581268,"cache_creation_input_tokens":911,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":911},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CcUMvBpzPs36stzn5XtVh","type":"assistant","uuid":"230ce9ae-fe31-4281-9141-4d93ef0e854f","timestamp":"2026-06-27T20:02:37.221Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\OneDrive\\binary16\\prime-silo","sessionId":"2273c372-b009-4668-8ae4-e7ffd0aad7d6","version":"2.1.187","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
